WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.100
-Also, it is a very
exciting week

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.000
for us here at "Late Night"
because Fred Armisen

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.667
is back with us on the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:10.968
-And, Fred,
I share this

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.334
with the audience
any time you're here.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:15.701
I am always overwhelmed
by how many different projects

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.501
you have going at one time,

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:20.200
and then you also
do things not for you,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.734
not to enrich yourself
financially or artistically,

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.234
but for other people.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.667
And I heard you're doing
an incredible thing.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:30.167
You are counterprogramming
Halloween for kids

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.367
who don't like trick
or treating.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.801
-Finally, yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.767
-So I'm doing something
where kids

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:41.234
can start rehearsing
for other holidays.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:44.167
Like, you know,
Christmas or Hanukkah

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:45.767
or Easter or whatever it is,

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:48.133
they could start
just doing a rehearsal

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.067
just to get ready
for birthdays and things.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.901
The problem is
kids aren't ready.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.801
-Okay.
-So we bring them --

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:56.067
-They, like, sort of get
caught off guard, say, by like,

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:58.200
hey, it's Thanksgiving.
And they're like...

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.767
-Yes, that's exactly
what I mean.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:01.968
So, like, let's sit
around a table,

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.300
let's have imaginary food.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.200
Let's kind of like
go through it

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.901
so you're not nervous about it,
and it goes for birthdays, too.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.567
Do you know how to say
happy birthday to someone?

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:10.767
Do you know how to like...?

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:12.033
-Oh, so it's not
just for your birthday,

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.734
but if you get invited
to a birthday,

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:14.901
you can rehearse for that.

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.400
-It just takes away
the nervousness.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.601
-Yeah.
-So when they come --

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.667
-This is something that you're
doing uniquely

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:20.901
on October 31st,

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.167
if you don't want
to trick or treat,

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.434
you go to --
where do you go?

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.200
-So, it's in Central Park.
-Okay.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.300
-And so there's a --
there's like all these

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.834
bicycle rentals there,
and it's just right next to it.

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:34.033
But please don't crowd in
because all the tourists

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.734
are trying to grab the bicycles.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.167
So we're just asking everyone
to like please, please,

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:41.167
please move over.
There's like an area

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.534
that has like a little bit
of grass and cement.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:44.968
Please don't crowd the bicycles.

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:46.400
We're just asking.
-Now, why?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.234
You seem so concerned
about crowding

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.367
the bicycle rack,
why would you do it?

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:53.167
Why would you set up there?
Because you're almost talking

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.067
more about the bicycle
rack situation

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.901
than you are about
the actual holiday rehearsal.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.501
-It's just because
they get so mad.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.367
The people who rent out
the bikes are always kind of

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:02.767
like they take it out on me

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.267
and they start yelling at me
about it,

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:07.501
and I'm like, I can't hand--
You know, these are kids.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.934
You know what I mean?

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.667
So kids, they
just wander around,

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.100
and we're just asking, please,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.000
just stay on the cement,
just stay on the pavement

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.701
and we could do
the rehearsals from there.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:17.901
-Okay, great.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.467
And if people
want to learn more about this,

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.868
is there a website
they can go to?

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.834
-No, but I asked them
to talk to you.

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:25.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.167
-Give it up for
Fred Armisen, everybody.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.834
-Thank you.
Thank you.

